According to a latest report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Power Line Carrier Communication Equipment Market was valued at USD 1.92 billion in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 2.98 billion by 2031, expanding at a CAGR of 7.4% during the forecast period. The market is being driven by increasing smart-grid deployments, growing industrial automation, modernization of electricity infrastructure, rising demand for cost-effective communication networks, and the ability of power-line communication technologies to transmit data through existing electrical wiring without requiring dedicated communication cabling.
Power Line Carrier Communication (PLCC) equipment enables high-frequency communication signals to be transmitted over existing power-line infrastructure. Core equipment includes modems, couplers, filters, repeaters, and related communication components designed for utility, industrial, commercial, and residential applications. The technology provides an important communication option for smart meters, grid monitoring, industrial automation, and connected-home applications.
